    {"problem": "Repair bills now show up every year", "solution": "When an older furnace needs a control board one winter and an inducer the next, the money adds up fast. We put the repair price beside a replacement price, so you decide with real numbers instead of a hunch."},
    {"problem": "Your AC and furnace went in the same year as the drywall", "solution": "Equipment installed together tends to fail close together. Replacing both at once lets you swap the AC for a heat pump that cools in summer and heats most of the winter, with one outdoor unit doing both jobs."},
    {"problem": "The gas bill creeps up while the thermostat stays put", "solution": "Older mid-efficiency furnaces send more of each cubic metre of gas up the vent. A 96% AFUE two-stage furnace, or a hybrid that leans on the heat pump, cuts the gas you burn."},
